/-!
# Coprimality certificates for `Φ₃` and `ΨSq₃` on the note's explicit curves

Discharges `IsCoprime (W.Φ 3) (W.ΨSq 3)` for the Weierstrass model of note eq. (3.7)
over `ℚ(z)`, yielding an unconditional degree-nine statement via `finrank_mulThreeX`.

The Bézout pair is generated by the extended Euclidean algorithm over `ℚ(z)`, cleared of
denominators as `D = z⁴ · q₈(z)²`, and checked as an identity in `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℚ`
by `ring`. Since `ΨSq 3 = Ψ₃²`, coprimality with `Ψ₃` plus `IsCoprime.pow_right` yields the
claim for `ΨSq 3`.

The companion model (5.6) over `ℚ(t)(λ)` is not included here: the same method applies
(cleared witnesses are small — `U` of degree 3 and `V` of degree 8 in `X`, with common
denominator `5184 λ⁴ q₋² q₊²`), but was deprioritized after the degree-nine corollary for
(3.7) was obtained.
-/

set_option maxHeartbeats 800000

noncomputable section

open MvPolynomial
open scoped IntermediateField

namespace ExplicitUnirational

/-! ## Arithmetic surface over `ℚ(z)` (note (3.7)) -/

/-- Base field `ℚ(z)` for the model (3.7). -/
public abbrev KQ : Type := RatFunc ℚ

/-- The quartic `P(z)` of note eq. (3.5). -/
public noncomputable def noteP : KQ :=
  4 * RatFunc.X ^ 4 - 23 * RatFunc.X ^ 3 - 18 * RatFunc.X ^ 2 + RatFunc.X - 4

/-- The short Weierstrass model of note eq. (3.7) over `ℚ(z)`. -/
public noncomputable def noteCurveQ : WeierstrassCurve KQ where
  a₁ := 0
  a₂ := 0
  a₃ := 0
  a₄ := RatFunc.X ^ 2 * (3 - RatFunc.X)
  a₆ := (RatFunc.X / 4) * noteP

